   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Evaluación Profunda — Fase 2 (BLIP-2 dual-LoRA · MIMIC-CXR 50 %)\n",
    "\n",
    "Notebook de evaluación **cualitativa** y **diagnóstica** del modelo `Config_B1` (LLM r=32 + ViT r=8) entrenado con el 50 % del dataset.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Sección 1 — Inferencia Cualitativa Visual:** carga el modelo dual-LoRA, genera reportes para 10 estudios aleatorios del test set y los compara visualmente (imagen + *Ground Truth* vs. *Generado*), calculando métricas de texto (BLEU-4, ROUGE-L, F1-RadGraph) **y clínicas (CheXpert/CheXbert)** con el **mismo pipeline que `evaluate_final.py`**.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Sección 2 — Sanity Check del ViT (Linear Probing):** aísla el ViT con sus pesos LoRA **fusionados**, lo **congela al 100 %**, y entrena una capa lineal sobre el token CLS con las 14 etiquetas CheXpert (`BCEWithLogitsLoss`) para confirmar — vía **AUC-ROC** — que el ViT sigue extrayendo características clínicas de alto nivel. *(Estructura idéntica a `vit_sanity_check.py`.)*\n",
    "\n",
    "> ⚠️ **Requisito:** el entrenamiento masivo debe estar **pausado** para liberar la VRAM de la L40S (~45 GB libres)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "448a37e5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 0 · Configuración e Imports"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "e07c902e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "ename": "",
     "evalue": "",
     "output_type": "error",
     "traceback": [
      "\u001b[1;31mRunning cells with 'Python 3.10.12' requires the ipykernel package.\n",
      "\u001b[1;31m<a href='command:jupyter.createPythonEnvAndSelectController'>Create a Python Environment</a> with the required packages.\n",
      "\u001b[1;31mOr install 'ipykernel' using the command: '/usr/bin/python3.10 -m pip install ipykernel -U --user --force-reinstall'"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# ── Imports base ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "import gc\n",
    "import math\n",
    "import random\n",
    "import textwrap\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import torch\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from PIL import Image\n",
    "from tqdm.auto import tqdm\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Módulos del proyecto (arquitectura modular) ───────────────────────────────\n",
    "from config import config\n",
    "from model_utils import cargar_procesador\n",
    "from data_loader import MimicCXRDataset\n",
    "from preprocessing import estandarizar_imagen\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Reproducibilidad ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "SEED = 42\n",
    "random.seed(SEED)\n",
    "np.random.seed(SEED)\n",
    "torch.manual_seed(SEED)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Rutas (Fase 2 · 50 %) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "BASE_DIR       = config.paths.base_dir\n",
    "BEST_MODEL_DIR = BASE_DIR / \"phase2_results-50pct\" / \"checkpoints\" / \"best_model_Config_B1\"\n",
    "TEST_CSV       = BASE_DIR / \"test_split_50pct.csv\"\n",
    "TRAIN_CSV      = BASE_DIR / \"train_split_50pct.csv\"\n",
    "VAL_CSV        = BASE_DIR / \"val_split_50pct.csv\"\n",
    "IMAGES_DIR     = BASE_DIR / \"imagenes_50_porciento\"\n",
    "CHEXPERT_CSV   = BASE_DIR / \"mimic-cxr-2.0.0-chexpert.csv\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Adaptadores duales (formato best_model: subdirectorios llm/ + vit/)\n",
    "LLM_DIR = BEST_MODEL_DIR / \"llm\"\n",
    "VIT_DIR = BEST_MODEL_DIR / \"vit\"\n",
    "\n",
    "DEVICE = torch.device(\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\")\n",
    "\n",
    "assert LLM_DIR.exists(), f\"No existe el adaptador LLM: {LLM_DIR}\"\n",
    "assert VIT_DIR.exists(), f\"No existe el adaptador ViT: {VIT_DIR}\"\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Modelo base : {config.model.model_name}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Best model  : {BEST_MODEL_DIR.name}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  ├─ LLM LoRA: {LLM_DIR}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  └─ ViT LoRA: {VIT_DIR}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Device      : {DEVICE}\")\n",
    "if torch.cuda.is_available():\n",
    "    print(f\"VRAM libre  : {torch.cuda.mem_get_info()[0] / 1e9:.1f} GB / \"\n",
    "          f\"{torch.cuda.get_device_properties(0).total_memory / 1e9:.1f} GB\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "78bb80d5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1 · Inferencia Cualitativa Visual (10 muestras)\n",
    "\n",
    "Carga el modelo **dual-LoRA** y genera reportes con los hiperparámetros **estrictos** solicitados:\n",
    "`max_new_tokens=512`, `repetition_penalty=1.2`, `num_beams=5`.\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Detalle técnico clave:** el adaptador del **LLM** se mantiene como `PeftModel`, pero el del **ViT** se **fusiona** con `merge_and_unload()`. Durante `generate()`, BLIP-2 invoca `vision_model(pixel_values, …)` de forma *posicional*; un wrapper `PeftModel` rompería esa llamada (mapearía el argumento al nombre `input_ids`). Fusionar los deltas LoRA devuelve un `Blip2VisionModel` nativo que funciona sin parches. *(Patrón idéntico al de `run_tournament.py`.)*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7503ccd1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def cargar_modelo_dual_lora(best_model_dir: Path, device_map: str = \"auto\"):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Carga BLIP-2 base en bfloat16 e inyecta AMBOS adaptadores LoRA de Fase 2.\n",
    "\n",
    "    - LLM  → PeftModel (se mantiene el wrapper; generate() lo usa internamente).\n",
    "    - ViT  → merge_and_unload() (fusión OBLIGATORIA: generate() llama al ViT con\n",
    "             pixel_values posicional, incompatible con el wrapper PeftModel).\n",
    "\n",
    "    Returns\n",
    "    -------\n",
    "    (model, device) — modelo en eval() listo para generate().\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    from transformers import Blip2ForConditionalGeneration\n",
    "    from peft import PeftModel\n",
    "\n",
    "    llm_dir = Path(best_model_dir) / \"llm\"\n",
    "    vit_dir = Path(best_model_dir) / \"vit\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    print(\"Cargando modelo base BLIP-2 (bfloat16)…\")\n",
    "    base_model = Blip2ForConditionalGeneration.from_pretrained(\n",
    "        config.model.model_name,\n",
    "        torch_dtype=torch.bfloat16,\n",
    "        device_map=device_map,\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    print(\"Inyectando LLM LoRA (is_trainable=False)…\")\n",
    "    base_model.language_model = PeftModel.from_pretrained(\n",
    "        base_model.language_model, str(llm_dir), is_trainable=False\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    print(\"Inyectando ViT LoRA y fusionando (merge_and_unload)…\")\n",
    "    vit_peft = PeftModel.from_pretrained(\n",
    "        base_model.vision_model, str(vit_dir), is_trainable=False\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    # qformer nunca se toca → refleja el device/dtype reales del modelo base\n",
    "    _ref = next(base_model.qformer.parameters())\n",
    "    base_model.vision_model = vit_peft.merge_and_unload().to(\n",
    "        device=_ref.device, dtype=_ref.dtype\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    base_model.eval()\n",
    "    print(f\"✅ Modelo dual-LoRA en {_ref.device} | dtype={_ref.dtype}\")\n",
    "    return base_model, _ref.device\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# Procesador (tokenizer + image processor) y modelo\n",
    "processor = cargar_procesador(model_name=config.model.model_name)\n",
    "model, device = cargar_modelo_dual_lora(BEST_MODEL_DIR, device_map=\"auto\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "34fe18ef",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Hiperparámetros de generación ESTRICTOS (solicitados)\n",
    "GEN_PARAMS = dict(\n",
    "    max_new_tokens     = 512,\n",
    "    repetition_penalty = 1.2,\n",
    "    num_beams          = 5,\n",
    "    do_sample          = False,   # beam search determinista\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Dataset de test — lo usamos para _buscar_imagen() y _mapear_vista()\n",
    "test_dataset = MimicCXRDataset(\n",
    "    csv_path             = TEST_CSV,\n",
    "    images_dir           = IMAGES_DIR,\n",
    "    processor            = processor,\n",
    "    image_size           = config.data.image_size,\n",
    "    clahe_clip_limit     = config.data.clahe_clip_limit,\n",
    "    clahe_tile_grid_size = config.data.clahe_tile_grid_size,\n",
    "    max_length           = config.data.max_length,\n",
    "    padding              = config.data.padding,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# 10 estudios aleatorios\n",
    "N_MUESTRAS = 10\n",
    "indices = random.sample(range(len(test_dataset)), N_MUESTRAS)\n",
    "print(f\"Test set: {len(test_dataset):,} estudios | seleccionados: {indices}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "@torch.inference_mode()\n",
    "def generar_reporte(idx: int) -> dict:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Genera el reporte para una fila del test set; devuelve imagen + textos.\"\"\"\n",
    "    row      = test_dataset.data.iloc[idx]\n",
    "    dicom_id = str(row[\"dicom_id\"])\n",
    "    study_id = str(row.get(\"study_id\", \"\"))\n",
    "    ref_text = str(row[\"report_text\"]).strip()\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Prompt dinámico con metadato de vista (idéntico a evaluate_final.py)\n",
    "    view_raw = row.get(\"ViewPosition\", None)\n",
    "    if view_raw is not None and not (isinstance(view_raw, float) and math.isnan(view_raw)):\n",
    "        vista = test_dataset._mapear_vista(str(view_raw))\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        vista = \"Unknown\"\n",
    "    prompt = f\"[Context: {vista} view] {config.inference.default_prompt}\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Preprocesado idéntico al de entrenamiento (CLAHE + resize + normalización)\n",
    "    imagen_path = test_dataset._buscar_imagen(dicom_id)\n",
    "    imagen_pil  = estandarizar_imagen(\n",
    "        imagen_path,\n",
    "        target_size          = config.data.image_size,\n",
    "        clahe_clip_limit     = config.data.clahe_clip_limit,\n",
    "        clahe_tile_grid_size = config.data.clahe_tile_grid_size,\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    inputs        = processor(images=imagen_pil, text=prompt, return_tensors=\"pt\").to(device)\n",
    "    generated_ids = model.generate(**inputs, **GEN_PARAMS)\n",
    "    generado      = processor.batch_decode(generated_ids, skip_special_tokens=True)[0].strip()\n",
    "\n",
    "    return {\n",
    "        \"dicom_id\":   dicom_id,\n",
    "        \"study_id\":   study_id,\n",
    "        \"vista\":      vista,\n",
    "        \"imagen\":     imagen_pil,\n",
    "        \"referencia\": ref_text,\n",
    "        \"generado\":   generado,\n",
    "    }"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "ed72eef4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Generar los 10 reportes\n",
    "resultados = []\n",
    "for idx in tqdm(indices, desc=\"Generando reportes\", unit=\"estudio\"):\n",
    "    resultados.append(generar_reporte(idx))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"✅ {len(resultados)} reportes generados.\\n\")\n",
    "print(\"EJEMPLO ─ Estudio 1 (generado):\\n\")\n",
    "print(resultados[0][\"generado\"][:600])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3cb403e6",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def _wrap(texto: str, w: int = 88) -> str:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Envuelve el texto respetando saltos de línea originales.\"\"\"\n",
    "    lineas = texto.splitlines() or [texto]\n",
    "    return \"\\n\".join(textwrap.fill(l, w) if l.strip() else \"\" for l in lineas)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def mostrar_comparativa(resultados):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Una figura por estudio: radiografía (izq) + GT vs Generado (der).\"\"\"\n",
    "    for i, r in enumerate(resultados, 1):\n",
    "        fig, (ax_img, ax_txt) = plt.subplots(\n",
    "            1, 2, figsize=(15, 6), gridspec_kw={\"width_ratios\": [1, 1.7]}\n",
    "        )\n",
    "\n",
    "        # ── Radiografía ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "        ax_img.imshow(r[\"imagen\"], cmap=\"gray\")\n",
    "        ax_img.set_title(f\"Estudio {i} · {r['vista']} view\\n{r['dicom_id'][:18]}…\",\n",
    "                         fontsize=11, fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "        ax_img.axis(\"off\")\n",
    "\n",
    "        # ── Comparación de reportes (bloque único anclado arriba) ────────────\n",
    "        ax_txt.axis(\"off\")\n",
    "        bloque = (\n",
    "            f\"📋 GROUND TRUTH (Original)\\n{'─' * 72}\\n{_wrap(r['referencia'])}\"\n",
    "            f\"\\n\\n\\n🤖 GENERADO (beams=5 · rep_pen=1.2)\\n{'─' * 72}\\n{_wrap(r['generado'])}\"\n",
    "        )\n",
    "        ax_txt.text(0.0, 0.99, bloque, va=\"top\", ha=\"left\",\n",
    "                    fontsize=8.5, family=\"monospace\", transform=ax_txt.transAxes)\n",
    "\n",
    "        plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "        plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "mostrar_comparativa(resultados)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "df51be92",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1.1 · Métricas de Texto\n",
    "\n",
    "Calculadas sobre los 10 reportes generados con el **mismo pipeline que `evaluate_final.py`**:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Métrica | Qué mide |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| **BLEU-4** | Solapamiento de n-gramas (1–4) con suavizado de Chen-Cherry |\n",
    "| **ROUGE-L** | F-measure de la subsecuencia común más larga |\n",
    "| **F1-RadGraph** | Solapamiento de entidades/relaciones clínicas (`radgraph-xl`, `reward_level=\"all\"` → RG_ERbar) |\n",
    "\n",
    "> F1-RadGraph descarga el modelo `radgraph-xl` la primera vez (puede tardar). Si la librería no está instalada, la celda continúa sin esa métrica."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "4c123bf1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Parche de compatibilidad para RadGraph (ANTES de importar radgraph) ───────\n",
    "from transformers import PreTrainedTokenizerBase\n",
    "\n",
    "if not hasattr(PreTrainedTokenizerBase, \"encode_plus\"):\n",
    "    def _ep(self, text, text_pair=None, add_special_tokens=True, padding=False,\n",
    "            truncation=False, max_length=None, stride=0, return_tensors=None, **kwargs):\n",
    "        return self.__call__(text, text_pair=text_pair, add_special_tokens=add_special_tokens,\n",
    "                             padding=padding, truncation=truncation, max_length=max_length,\n",
    "                             stride=stride, return_tensors=return_tensors, **kwargs)\n",
    "    PreTrainedTokenizerBase.encode_plus = _ep\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Helpers de métricas (idénticos a evaluate_final.py) ───────────────────────\n",
    "import nltk\n",
    "from nltk.translate.bleu_score import sentence_bleu, SmoothingFunction\n",
    "from rouge_score import rouge_scorer as _rouge_module\n",
    "\n",
    "nltk.download(\"punkt\", quiet=True)\n",
    "nltk.download(\"punkt_tab\", quiet=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "_rouge = _rouge_module.RougeScorer([\"rougeL\"], use_stemmer=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def bleu4(reference: str, hypothesis: str) -> float:\n",
    "    ref = nltk.word_tokenize(reference.lower())\n",
    "    hyp = nltk.word_tokenize(hypothesis.lower())\n",
    "    return sentence_bleu([ref], hyp, weights=(0.25, 0.25, 0.25, 0.25),\n",
    "                         smoothing_function=SmoothingFunction().method1)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def rouge_l(reference: str, hypothesis: str) -> float:\n",
    "    return _rouge.score(reference, hypothesis)[\"rougeL\"].fmeasure\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── F1-RadGraph (opcional; descarga radgraph-xl la primera vez) ───────────────\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    from radgraph import F1RadGraph\n",
    "    print(\"Cargando F1RadGraph (reward_level='all', model_type='radgraph-xl')…\")\n",
    "    _f1rg = F1RadGraph(reward_level=\"all\", model_type=\"radgraph-xl\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    def radgraph_f1(reference: str, hypothesis: str) -> float:\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            mean_reward, _, _, _ = _f1rg(refs=[reference], hyps=[hypothesis])\n",
    "            # reward_level='all' → mean_reward = (simple, partial, complete); [2]=RG_ERbar\n",
    "            if isinstance(mean_reward, (tuple, list)):\n",
    "                return float(mean_reward[2])\n",
    "            return float(mean_reward)\n",
    "        except Exception as exc:\n",
    "            print(f\"  RadGraph error: {exc}\")\n",
    "            return float(\"nan\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    _HAS_RADGRAPH = True\n",
    "    print(\"  F1RadGraph listo.\")\n",
    "except Exception as exc:\n",
    "    print(f\"⚠️ RadGraph no disponible ({exc}). Se omite F1-RadGraph.\")\n",
    "    _HAS_RADGRAPH = False"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "eaad272b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Calcular métricas fila por fila sobre los 10 reportes ─────────────────────\n",
    "filas = []\n",
    "for i, r in enumerate(tqdm(resultados, desc=\"Métricas\"), 1):\n",
    "    ref = r[\"referencia\"] or \"no findings\"\n",
    "    hyp = r[\"generado\"]   or \"no findings\"\n",
    "    fila = {\n",
    "        \"estudio\":  i,\n",
    "        \"dicom_id\": r[\"dicom_id\"][:12],\n",
    "        \"BLEU-4\":   bleu4(ref, hyp),\n",
    "        \"ROUGE-L\":  rouge_l(ref, hyp),\n",
    "    }\n",
    "    if _HAS_RADGRAPH:\n",
    "        fila[\"F1-RadGraph\"] = radgraph_f1(ref, hyp)\n",
    "    filas.append(fila)\n",
    "\n",
    "df_metricas = pd.DataFrame(filas)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Tabla formateada\n",
    "_num_cols = [c for c in df_metricas.columns if c not in (\"estudio\", \"dicom_id\")]\n",
    "display(df_metricas.style.format({c: \"{:.4f}\" for c in _num_cols})\n",
    "                        .background_gradient(cmap=\"Greens\", subset=_num_cols))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Promedios globales (mismo espíritu que metricas_globales_comparacion.csv)\n",
    "print(\"\\nPROMEDIOS (10 muestras):\")\n",
    "for col in (\"BLEU-4\", \"ROUGE-L\", \"F1-RadGraph\"):\n",
    "    if col in df_metricas.columns:\n",
    "        print(f\"  {col:<12}: {df_metricas[col].mean():.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "bf5bec96",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1.2 · Evaluación Clínica con CheXpert\n",
    "\n",
    "Compara las **etiquetas clínicas** del CSV oficial (`mimic-cxr-2.0.0-chexpert.csv`, *Ground Truth*) contra las que **CheXbert** (Stanford AIMI) extrae de cada **reporte generado** — exactamente la Fase 2 de `evaluate_final.py`.\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Ground Truth:** *merge* por `study_id` con el CSV oficial de CheXpert.\n",
    "- **Predicho:** CheXbert etiqueta el `generated_report` en las 14 categorías.\n",
    "- **Binarización (idéntica a `evaluate_final.py`):** `1.0`/`-1.0` (incierto) → positivo; `0.0`/`NaN` → negativo.\n",
    "- **Métricas:** micro **Precision / Recall / F1** por estudio + *agreement* por clase, promediados al final."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "2cd281a2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from chexbert_official import CheXbertLabeler, CHEXBERT_LABELS\n",
    "\n",
    "_CHEX_COLS   = CHEXBERT_LABELS          # 14 etiquetas (orden CheXbert)\n",
    "_PRED_PREFIX = \"pred_chexpert_\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── GT oficial + labeler CheXbert (pesos cacheados en ~/.cache) ───────────────\n",
    "print(\"Cargando CheXbert oficial (Stanford AIMI)…\")\n",
    "chexbert   = CheXbertLabeler()          # autodetecta GPU/CPU\n",
    "df_chex_gt = pd.read_csv(CHEXPERT_CSV)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _norm_sid(s):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Normaliza study_id ('s5069...' o 5069...) → '5069...'.\"\"\"\n",
    "    s = str(s).strip()\n",
    "    return s.lstrip(\"s\") if s.startswith(\"s\") else s\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "df_chex_gt[\"_sid\"] = df_chex_gt[\"study_id\"].astype(str).apply(_norm_sid)\n",
    "_gt_by_sid = df_chex_gt.set_index(\"_sid\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Helpers idénticos a evaluate_final.py ─────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "def _chexpert_pred_cols(labeler, report):\n",
    "    \"\"\"CheXbert sobre el reporte generado → dict con prefijo pred_chexpert_.\"\"\"\n",
    "    raw = labeler.label(report)\n",
    "    return {f\"{_PRED_PREFIX}{lbl.lower().replace(' ', '_')}\": v for lbl, v in raw.items()}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _to_bin(v):\n",
    "    \"\"\"1.0/-1.0 (incierto)=mencionado→1 ; 0.0→0 ; NaN→None (no mencionado).\"\"\"\n",
    "    if isinstance(v, float) and math.isnan(v):\n",
    "        return None\n",
    "    return 1 if float(v) != 0.0 else 0\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _chexpert_comparison_metrics(gt_row, pred_dict):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Compara GT (CSV oficial) vs Pred (CheXbert) → micro P/R/F1 + match por clase.\"\"\"\n",
    "    tp = fp = fn = 0\n",
    "    m = {}\n",
    "    for lbl in _CHEX_COLS:\n",
    "        gt_val   = gt_row.get(lbl, float(\"nan\")) if gt_row is not None else float(\"nan\")\n",
    "        pred_val = pred_dict.get(f\"{_PRED_PREFIX}{lbl.lower().replace(' ', '_')}\", float(\"nan\"))\n",
    "        gt_bin, pred_bin = _to_bin(gt_val), _to_bin(pred_val)\n",
    "\n",
    "        key = f\"match_{lbl.lower().replace(' ', '_')}\"\n",
    "        if gt_bin is None and pred_bin is None:\n",
    "            m[key] = float(\"nan\")\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        if gt_bin   is None: gt_bin   = 0      # imputar no-mencionado = negativo\n",
    "        if pred_bin is None: pred_bin = 0\n",
    "        m[key] = 1.0 if gt_bin == pred_bin else 0.0\n",
    "\n",
    "        if   gt_bin == 1 and pred_bin == 1: tp += 1\n",
    "        elif gt_bin == 0 and pred_bin == 1: fp += 1\n",
    "        elif gt_bin == 1 and pred_bin == 0: fn += 1\n",
    "\n",
    "    precision = tp / (tp + fp) if (tp + fp) > 0 else float(\"nan\")\n",
    "    recall    = tp / (tp + fn) if (tp + fn) > 0 else float(\"nan\")\n",
    "    f1 = (2 * precision * recall / (precision + recall)\n",
    "          if not (math.isnan(precision) or math.isnan(recall)) and (precision + recall) > 0\n",
    "          else float(\"nan\"))\n",
    "    m[\"chexpert_precision\"] = precision\n",
    "    m[\"chexpert_recall\"]    = recall\n",
    "    m[\"chexpert_f1\"]        = f1\n",
    "    return m\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Evaluar los 10 reportes ───────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "filas_chex  = []\n",
    "match_accum = {l: [] for l in _CHEX_COLS}\n",
    "n_sin_gt    = 0\n",
    "\n",
    "for i, r in enumerate(tqdm(resultados, desc=\"CheXpert\"), 1):\n",
    "    sid = _norm_sid(r[\"study_id\"])\n",
    "    if sid in _gt_by_sid.index:\n",
    "        gt_row = _gt_by_sid.loc[sid]\n",
    "        if isinstance(gt_row, pd.DataFrame):      # study_id duplicado → 1ª fila\n",
    "            gt_row = gt_row.iloc[0]\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        gt_row = None\n",
    "        n_sin_gt += 1\n",
    "\n",
    "    pred = _chexpert_pred_cols(chexbert, r[\"generado\"] or \"no findings\")\n",
    "    cmp  = _chexpert_comparison_metrics(gt_row, pred)\n",
    "\n",
    "    filas_chex.append({\n",
    "        \"estudio\":   i,\n",
    "        \"study_id\":  r[\"study_id\"],\n",
    "        \"precision\": cmp[\"chexpert_precision\"],\n",
    "        \"recall\":    cmp[\"chexpert_recall\"],\n",
    "        \"f1\":        cmp[\"chexpert_f1\"],\n",
    "    })\n",
    "    for l in _CHEX_COLS:\n",
    "        v = cmp.get(f\"match_{l.lower().replace(' ', '_')}\", float(\"nan\"))\n",
    "        if not (isinstance(v, float) and math.isnan(v)):\n",
    "            match_accum[l].append(v)\n",
    "\n",
    "df_chexpert = pd.DataFrame(filas_chex)\n",
    "display(df_chexpert.style.format({c: \"{:.4f}\" for c in (\"precision\", \"recall\", \"f1\")}))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Promedios micro (sobre estudios con match)\n",
    "print(f\"\\nEstudios sin GT CheXpert (sin match por study_id): {n_sin_gt}/{len(resultados)}\")\n",
    "print(\"PROMEDIOS CheXpert (micro, por estudio):\")\n",
    "for col in (\"precision\", \"recall\", \"f1\"):\n",
    "    print(f\"  {col:<10}: {df_chexpert[col].mean(skipna=True):.4f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Agreement por clase (qué hallazgos clínicos acierta el modelo)\n",
    "df_agreement = (pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"clase\":     list(match_accum.keys()),\n",
    "    \"agreement\": [np.mean(v) if v else float(\"nan\") for v in match_accum.values()],\n",
    "    \"n_eval\":    [len(v) for v in match_accum.values()],\n",
    "}).sort_values(\"agreement\", ascending=False).reset_index(drop=True))\n",
    "print(\"\\nAGREEMENT por clase (GT vs Generado):\")\n",
    "display(df_agreement.style.format({\"agreement\": \"{:.3f}\"}))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "e6b0ef80",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Liberar el modelo de generación antes del Sanity Check del ViT ────────────\n",
    "# (deja libre la VRAM para volver a cargar BLIP-2 y aislar el ViT).\n",
    "del model\n",
    "gc.collect()\n",
    "if torch.cuda.is_available():\n",
    "    torch.cuda.empty_cache()\n",
    "    print(f\"Modelo liberado. VRAM libre: {torch.cuda.mem_get_info()[0] / 1e9:.1f} GB\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "281e0487",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2 · Sanity Check del ViT — Linear Probing\n",
    "\n",
    "Réplica fiel de `vit_sanity_check.py`. Aísla el **ViT** con sus pesos LoRA de Fase 2 **fusionados**, lo **congela al 100 %**, y entrena una única capa `nn.Linear` sobre el **token CLS** para predecir las 14 etiquetas CheXpert (multi-label, `BCEWithLogitsLoss`, `AdamW` lr=1e-3 wd=1e-4).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Optimización de VRAM (para que no colapse):**\n",
    "1. BLIP-2 se carga en **CPU**; se extrae solo `vision_model` y se **descarta** el resto (LLM 2.7B, Q-Former, projection).\n",
    "2. Se fusiona el LoRA (`merge_and_unload`) y se congela el ViT (`requires_grad=False`).\n",
    "3. Se **pre-extraen los embeddings una sola vez** (token CLS) y se cachean en RAM (CPU).\n",
    "4. El ViT se **libera de la VRAM**; el entrenamiento de la capa lineal corre sobre tensores cacheados (instantáneo).\n",
    "\n",
    "Un **AUC-ROC** alto confirma que el ViT sigue extrayendo características clínicas tras el fine-tuning con el 50 % de los datos.\n",
    "\n",
    "> Para una corrida **idéntica** a `vit_sanity_check.py` (dataset completo, sin submuestreo), pon `N_PROBE_TRAIN = N_PROBE_VAL = None` en la celda de ejecución."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a7085ee5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import torch.nn as nn\n",
    "from torch.optim import AdamW\n",
    "from torch.utils.data import Dataset, DataLoader\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import roc_auc_score, f1_score\n",
    "\n",
    "# 14 etiquetas CheXpert (orden del CSV oficial — idéntico a vit_sanity_check.py)\n",
    "CHEXPERT_LABELS = [\n",
    "    \"Atelectasis\", \"Cardiomegaly\", \"Consolidation\", \"Edema\",\n",
    "    \"Enlarged Cardiomediastinum\", \"Fracture\", \"Lung Lesion\", \"Lung Opacity\",\n",
    "    \"No Finding\", \"Pleural Effusion\", \"Pleural Other\", \"Pneumonia\",\n",
    "    \"Pneumothorax\", \"Support Devices\",\n",
    "]\n",
    "N_CLASSES    = len(CHEXPERT_LABELS)\n",
    "OUTPUT_DIR   = BASE_DIR / \"vit_sanity_check_results\"\n",
    "VIT_LORA_DIR = VIT_DIR     # phase2_results-50pct/.../best_model_Config_B1/vit\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "class CheXpertLabeledDataset(Dataset):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Envuelve MimicCXRDataset y añade etiquetas multi-label CheXpert.\n",
    "    Política U-ones (estándar CheXpert): -1 (incierto) → 1 ; 1 → 1 ; 0/NaN → 0.\n",
    "    Solo se incluyen muestras con study_id presente en el CSV de CheXpert.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    def __init__(self, base_dataset, chexpert_df):\n",
    "        base_df = base_dataset.data.copy()\n",
    "        base_df[\"_idx\"] = range(len(base_df))\n",
    "        base_df[\"study_id\"] = base_df[\"study_id\"].astype(str)\n",
    "        cx = chexpert_df.copy()\n",
    "        cx[\"study_id\"] = cx[\"study_id\"].astype(str)\n",
    "\n",
    "        merged = base_df.merge(cx[[\"study_id\"] + CHEXPERT_LABELS], on=\"study_id\", how=\"inner\")\n",
    "        merged = merged.dropna(subset=[\"_idx\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "        self.base_dataset = base_dataset\n",
    "        self.indices      = merged[\"_idx\"].tolist()\n",
    "        # U-ones explícito\n",
    "        raw = merged[CHEXPERT_LABELS].fillna(0).values.astype(np.float32)\n",
    "        self.labels = np.where(raw == -1.0, 1.0, np.where(raw == 1.0, 1.0, 0.0)).astype(np.float32)\n",
    "\n",
    "        print(f\"   CheXpertLabeledDataset: {len(self.indices):,} muestras con etiqueta \"\n",
    "              f\"({len(base_df) - len(self.indices):,} sin match descartadas)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    def __len__(self):\n",
    "        return len(self.indices)\n",
    "\n",
    "    def __getitem__(self, idx):\n",
    "        sample       = self.base_dataset[self.indices[idx]]\n",
    "        pixel_values = sample[\"pixel_values\"]                       # [3, H, W]\n",
    "        labels       = torch.tensor(self.labels[idx], dtype=torch.float32)\n",
    "        return pixel_values, labels\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "class ViTLinearClassifier(nn.Module):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    ViT (EVA-CLIP de BLIP-2) congelado + capa lineal de 14 clases sobre el token CLS.\n",
    "    (Definido por fidelidad a vit_sanity_check.py; el flujo cacheado usa nn.Linear.)\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    def __init__(self, vit, hidden_size, n_classes=N_CLASSES):\n",
    "        super().__init__()\n",
    "        self.vit        = vit\n",
    "        self.classifier = nn.Linear(hidden_size, n_classes)\n",
    "\n",
    "    def forward(self, pixel_values):\n",
    "        outputs = self.vit(pixel_values=pixel_values, return_dict=True)\n",
    "        if getattr(outputs, \"pooler_output\", None) is not None:\n",
    "            features = outputs.pooler_output\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            features = outputs.last_hidden_state[:, 0, :]           # token CLS\n",
    "        return self.classifier(features.float())\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "class FeatureDataset(Dataset):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Sirve embeddings ViT pre-extraídos (CPU, float32). El ViT no vuelve a ejecutarse.\"\"\"\n",
    "    def __init__(self, features, labels):\n",
    "        self.features = features\n",
    "        self.labels   = labels\n",
    "\n",
    "    def __len__(self):\n",
    "        return len(self.features)\n",
    "\n",
    "    def __getitem__(self, idx):\n",
    "        return self.features[idx], self.labels[idx]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d8e2ab04",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def load_vit_phase2(vit_lora_dir, device):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Carga BLIP-2 en CPU, extrae el ViT, fusiona el LoRA de Fase 2 y lo congela.\n",
    "    VRAM-opt: descarta LLM/Q-Former/projection ANTES de mover el ViT a GPU.\n",
    "    Returns (vit, hidden_size).\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    from transformers import Blip2ForConditionalGeneration\n",
    "    from peft import PeftModel\n",
    "\n",
    "    print(\"  Cargando BLIP-2 completo en CPU para extraer el ViT…\")\n",
    "    full_model = Blip2ForConditionalGeneration.from_pretrained(\n",
    "        config.model.model_name, torch_dtype=torch.bfloat16, device_map=\"cpu\",\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    vit = full_model.vision_model\n",
    "    hidden_size = vit.config.hidden_size\n",
    "    print(f\"  ViT extraído: hidden_size={hidden_size}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Descartar el resto del modelo (libera RAM)\n",
    "    del full_model.language_model\n",
    "    del full_model.qformer\n",
    "    del full_model.language_projection\n",
    "    del full_model\n",
    "    gc.collect()\n",
    "    if torch.cuda.is_available():\n",
    "        torch.cuda.empty_cache()\n",
    "    print(\"  Resto del modelo descartado (RAM liberada)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    if Path(vit_lora_dir).exists():\n",
    "        print(f\"  Cargando ViT LoRA de Fase 2 desde {vit_lora_dir}…\")\n",
    "        vit_peft = PeftModel.from_pretrained(vit, str(vit_lora_dir), is_trainable=False)\n",
    "        vit = vit_peft.merge_and_unload()\n",
    "        print(\"  LoRA fusionado (merge_and_unload) ✓\")\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print(f\"  ⚠️ ViT LoRA no encontrado: {vit_lora_dir} — usando ViT base (ablación)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Congelar TODO el ViT\n",
    "    for param in vit.parameters():\n",
    "        param.requires_grad = False\n",
    "    n_frozen = sum(p.numel() for p in vit.parameters())\n",
    "    print(f\"  ViT 100% congelado: {n_frozen:,} parámetros (requires_grad=False)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    vit = vit.to(device=device, dtype=torch.bfloat16)\n",
    "    return vit, hidden_size\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "@torch.inference_mode()\n",
    "def precompute_features(vit, dataset, batch_size, num_workers, device, split_name=\"\"):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Pasa TODO el dataset UNA vez por el ViT congelado y cachea embeddings (CLS) en RAM.\"\"\"\n",
    "    loader = DataLoader(\n",
    "        dataset, batch_size=batch_size * 2, shuffle=False,   # sin grad → batch mayor\n",
    "        num_workers=num_workers, pin_memory=True,\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    all_features, all_labels = [], []\n",
    "    vit.eval()\n",
    "    for pixel_values, labels in tqdm(loader, desc=f\"  Pre-extrayendo features [{split_name}]\"):\n",
    "        outputs = vit(pixel_values=pixel_values.to(device), return_dict=True)\n",
    "        if getattr(outputs, \"pooler_output\", None) is not None:\n",
    "            feats = outputs.pooler_output\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            feats = outputs.last_hidden_state[:, 0, :]\n",
    "        all_features.append(feats.float().cpu())\n",
    "        all_labels.append(labels.cpu())\n",
    "    features = torch.cat(all_features, dim=0)\n",
    "    labels   = torch.cat(all_labels,   dim=0)\n",
    "    print(f\"  Features [{split_name}]: {tuple(features.shape)}  labels: {tuple(labels.shape)}\")\n",
    "    return features, labels\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def compute_metrics(all_labels, all_probs, threshold=0.5):\n",
    "    \"\"\"AUC-ROC macro (clases con ≥2 valores presentes) + F1-macro (multi-label).\"\"\"\n",
    "    auc_scores = []\n",
    "    for i in range(all_labels.shape[1]):\n",
    "        col = all_labels[:, i]\n",
    "        if len(np.unique(col)) < 2:\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            auc_scores.append(roc_auc_score(col, all_probs[:, i]))\n",
    "        except Exception:\n",
    "            pass\n",
    "    auc_macro = float(np.mean(auc_scores)) if auc_scores else float(\"nan\")\n",
    "    preds     = (all_probs >= threshold).astype(int)\n",
    "    f1_macro  = f1_score(all_labels, preds, average=\"macro\", zero_division=0)\n",
    "    return auc_macro, f1_macro\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def train(model, train_loader, val_loader, epochs, lr, device, output_dir):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Entrena el clasificador lineal sobre features cacheadas.\n",
    "    Idéntico a vit_sanity_check.py: AdamW(wd=1e-4) + BCEWithLogitsLoss; guarda el mejor\n",
    "    por AUC-ROC y exporta history_vit_sanity_check.csv.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    optimizer = AdamW(model.parameters(), lr=lr, weight_decay=1e-4)\n",
    "    criterion = nn.BCEWithLogitsLoss()\n",
    "    print(f\"  Parámetros entrenables (clasificador lineal): \"\n",
    "          f\"{sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters()):,}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    history   = []\n",
    "    best_auc  = -1.0\n",
    "    best_path = output_dir / \"best_linear_classifier.pt\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    for epoch in range(1, epochs + 1):\n",
    "        # ── TRAIN ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "        model.train()\n",
    "        train_losses = []\n",
    "        for features, labels in tqdm(train_loader, desc=f\"  Epoch {epoch}/{epochs} [train]\", leave=False):\n",
    "            features, labels = features.to(device), labels.to(device)\n",
    "            optimizer.zero_grad()\n",
    "            loss = criterion(model(features), labels)\n",
    "            loss.backward()\n",
    "            optimizer.step()\n",
    "            train_losses.append(loss.item())\n",
    "        train_loss = float(np.mean(train_losses))\n",
    "\n",
    "        # ── VAL ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "        model.eval()\n",
    "        val_losses, all_labels, all_probs = [], [], []\n",
    "        with torch.no_grad():\n",
    "            for features, labels in tqdm(val_loader, desc=f\"  Epoch {epoch}/{epochs} [val]  \", leave=False):\n",
    "                features = features.to(device)\n",
    "                logits   = model(features)\n",
    "                val_losses.append(criterion(logits, labels.to(device)).item())\n",
    "                all_probs.append(torch.sigmoid(logits).cpu().numpy())\n",
    "                all_labels.append(labels.numpy())\n",
    "        val_loss   = float(np.mean(val_losses))\n",
    "        all_labels = np.concatenate(all_labels, axis=0)\n",
    "        all_probs  = np.concatenate(all_probs,  axis=0)\n",
    "        auc_macro, f1_macro = compute_metrics(all_labels, all_probs)\n",
    "\n",
    "        # Guardar el mejor clasificador\n",
    "        if not np.isnan(auc_macro) and auc_macro > best_auc:\n",
    "            best_auc = auc_macro\n",
    "            torch.save(model.state_dict(), best_path)\n",
    "            marker = \" ← best\"\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            marker = \"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "        print(f\"  Epoch {epoch:>2}/{epochs} | train_loss={train_loss:.4f}  \"\n",
    "              f\"val_loss={val_loss:.4f}  AUC-ROC={auc_macro:.4f}  F1-macro={f1_macro:.4f}{marker}\")\n",
    "        history.append({\"epoch\": epoch, \"train_loss\": train_loss, \"val_loss\": val_loss,\n",
    "                        \"auc_roc_macro\": auc_macro, \"f1_macro\": f1_macro})\n",
    "\n",
    "    df_history = pd.DataFrame(history)\n",
    "    df_history.to_csv(output_dir / \"history_vit_sanity_check.csv\", index=False)\n",
    "    print(f\"\\n  Historia → {output_dir / 'history_vit_sanity_check.csv'}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Mejor clasificador → {best_path}  (AUC-ROC={best_auc:.4f})\")\n",
    "    return df_history"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "60ef5c3d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Parámetros (idénticos a vit_sanity_check.py; subset para rapidez) ─────────\n",
    "EPOCHS        = 10\n",
    "BATCH_SIZE    = 64\n",
    "LR            = 1e-3\n",
    "NUM_WORKERS   = 4\n",
    "N_PROBE_TRAIN = 8000      # None → dataset completo (idéntico a vit_sanity_check.py)\n",
    "N_PROBE_VAL   = 3000\n",
    "\n",
    "OUTPUT_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Etiquetas CheXpert ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "chexpert_df = pd.read_csv(CHEXPERT_CSV)\n",
    "print(f\"Etiquetas CheXpert: {len(chexpert_df):,} estudios\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Datasets base (prompt='' → solo necesitamos pixel_values) ─────────────────\n",
    "shared_kwargs = dict(\n",
    "    images_dir           = IMAGES_DIR,\n",
    "    processor            = processor,\n",
    "    image_size           = config.data.image_size,\n",
    "    clahe_clip_limit     = config.data.clahe_clip_limit,\n",
    "    clahe_tile_grid_size = config.data.clahe_tile_grid_size,\n",
    "    max_length           = 512,\n",
    "    padding              = config.data.padding,\n",
    "    prompt               = \"\",\n",
    ")\n",
    "base_train = MimicCXRDataset(csv_path=TRAIN_CSV, **shared_kwargs)\n",
    "base_val   = MimicCXRDataset(csv_path=VAL_CSV,   **shared_kwargs)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Submuestreo para un probing rápido y ligero (N_PROBE_*=None → usar todo)\n",
    "if N_PROBE_TRAIN:\n",
    "    base_train.data = base_train.data.sample(\n",
    "        n=min(N_PROBE_TRAIN, len(base_train.data)), random_state=SEED).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "if N_PROBE_VAL:\n",
    "    base_val.data = base_val.data.sample(\n",
    "        n=min(N_PROBE_VAL, len(base_val.data)), random_state=SEED).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "train_ds = CheXpertLabeledDataset(base_train, chexpert_df)\n",
    "val_ds   = CheXpertLabeledDataset(base_val,   chexpert_df)\n",
    "print(f\"\\nTrain: {len(train_ds):,}  |  Val: {len(val_ds):,}\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Cargar ViT (VRAM-opt) y pre-extraer features (una sola pasada) ────────────\n",
    "vit, hidden_size = load_vit_phase2(VIT_LORA_DIR, DEVICE)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nPre-extrayendo embeddings del ViT (una sola vez)…\")\n",
    "train_feats, train_lbls = precompute_features(vit, train_ds, BATCH_SIZE, NUM_WORKERS, DEVICE, \"train\")\n",
    "val_feats,   val_lbls   = precompute_features(vit, val_ds,   BATCH_SIZE, NUM_WORKERS, DEVICE, \"val\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# ViT ya no se necesita en GPU → liberar VRAM\n",
    "del vit\n",
    "gc.collect()\n",
    "if torch.cuda.is_available():\n",
    "    torch.cuda.empty_cache()\n",
    "    print(f\"\\nViT liberado. VRAM libre: {torch.cuda.mem_get_info()[0]/1e9:.1f} GB\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "03dd4e22",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── DataLoaders sobre features cacheadas (tensors en RAM → num_workers=0) ──────\n",
    "train_loader = DataLoader(FeatureDataset(train_feats, train_lbls),\n",
    "                          batch_size=BATCH_SIZE, shuffle=True,  num_workers=0, pin_memory=True)\n",
    "val_loader   = DataLoader(FeatureDataset(val_feats,   val_lbls),\n",
    "                          batch_size=BATCH_SIZE, shuffle=False, num_workers=0, pin_memory=True)\n",
    "print(f\"Batches train: {len(train_loader):,}  |  val: {len(val_loader):,}\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Clasificador lineal (el ViT ya no está en el grafo) ───────────────────────\n",
    "clf_model = nn.Linear(hidden_size, N_CLASSES).to(DEVICE)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Entrenamiento (idéntico a vit_sanity_check.py) ────────────────────────────\n",
    "df_hist = train(\n",
    "    model        = clf_model,\n",
    "    train_loader = train_loader,\n",
    "    val_loader   = val_loader,\n",
    "    epochs       = EPOCHS,\n",
    "    lr           = LR,\n",
    "    device       = DEVICE,\n",
    "    output_dir   = OUTPUT_DIR,\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "0c244919",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Resumen final (idéntico a vit_sanity_check.py) ────────────────────────────\n",
    "best_row = df_hist.loc[df_hist[\"auc_roc_macro\"].idxmax()]\n",
    "auc_best = best_row[\"auc_roc_macro\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 65)\n",
    "print(\"  SANITY CHECK ViT — Linear Probing (CheXpert 14 clases)\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 65)\n",
    "print(f\"  Mejor época            : {int(best_row['epoch'])}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Mejor AUC-ROC macro    : {auc_best:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  F1-macro en esa época  : {best_row['f1_macro']:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Val loss mínima        : {df_hist['val_loss'].min():.4f}\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 65)\n",
    "if auc_best >= 0.75:\n",
    "    print(\"  ✅ El ViT extrae características clínicas de ALTO nivel.\")\n",
    "elif auc_best >= 0.65:\n",
    "    print(\"  🟡 El ViT extrae señal clínica MODERADA.\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"  🔴 Señal clínica débil — revisar el entrenamiento del ViT.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Curvas de entrenamiento ───────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(13, 4.5))\n",
    "ax[0].plot(df_hist[\"epoch\"], df_hist[\"train_loss\"], \"o-\", label=\"train\")\n",
    "ax[0].plot(df_hist[\"epoch\"], df_hist[\"val_loss\"],   \"s-\", label=\"val\")\n",
    "ax[0].set_title(\"Pérdida (BCEWithLogitsLoss)\")\n",
    "ax[0].set_xlabel(\"época\"); ax[0].set_ylabel(\"loss\"); ax[0].legend(); ax[0].grid(alpha=.3)\n",
    "\n",
    "ax[1].plot(df_hist[\"epoch\"], df_hist[\"auc_roc_macro\"], \"o-\", color=\"#1a9850\", label=\"AUC-ROC macro\")\n",
    "ax[1].plot(df_hist[\"epoch\"], df_hist[\"f1_macro\"],      \"s-\", color=\"#762a83\", label=\"F1-macro\")\n",
    "ax[1].axhline(0.75, ls=\"--\", color=\"gray\", alpha=.6)\n",
    "ax[1].set_title(\"Métricas de validación\")\n",
    "ax[1].set_xlabel(\"época\"); ax[1].set_ylim(0, 1); ax[1].legend(); ax[1].grid(alpha=.3)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
